cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PAD4-DB, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: dataset
title: "PAD4-DB: A curated structure-activity resource for PAD4 inhibitors with activity cliff characterization"
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-07-01"
doi: "TBD — will be updated after Zenodo deposition"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Nidhal212/PAD4-DB"
license: CC-BY-SA-4.0
abstract: >
  PAD4-DB is a curated database of 3,093 human PAD4 (peptidylarginine deiminase 4)
  inhibitors integrated from 95 PubChem bioassays, ChEMBL (CHEMBL6111), and BindingDB
  (UniProt Q9UM07). The database provides consensus pIC50 values, source independence
  scores, systematic activity cliff characterization (94 severe pairs, 85.1%
  MMP-confirmed), scaffold annotations (1,244 unique Murcko scaffolds), and cliff-hub
  labels for four compounds in two structural classes. A 327,336-compound HTS structural
  reference index is included. The full curation pipeline is implemented in Snakemake
  and reproduces all results from raw source data.
keywords:
  - PAD4
  - PADI4
  - peptidylarginine deiminase
  - PAD4 inhibitors
  - activity cliffs
  - structure-activity relationships
  - matched molecular pairs
  - scaffold analysis
  - bioactivity database
  - cheminformatics
  - drug discovery
  - machine learning benchmarks
